    phrases: [
      "Give me a moment — I want to write this one down before the table talks me out of what I actually thought.",
      "That fold was the right rate for the risk. What the river did after is a separate question.",
      "I'm not upset about the hand. I'm mildly upset that I enjoyed the bad call working.",
      "Two columns, gentlemen — decision and result. Tonight they disagree more than usual.",
      "That's four hands in a row you've won on the river. Charming. Also not a pattern yet.",
      "I priced that Anaconda low draw as a pass. The fact that it got there doesn't reprice it retroactively.",
      "My spreadsheet — sorry, notebook — says I've made this exact fold in this exact spot eleven times this year.",
      "It's not a bad beat. It's an unlucky outcome attached to a decision I'd make again tonight.",
      "I'll take the free enterprise wipe at this price. Two rounds from now, at double, I probably won't.",
      "You know what actuaries call a hot streak? Four claims. That's not a sample, that's a coincidence with a good publicist.",
      "I mucked correctly nine hands running. Nobody at this table noticed, which is sort of the point.",
      "Ask me again in a hundred hands. Right now you're asking me about noise.",
      "I don't feel sharper with a big stack. I feel sharper when I can tell you *why* the stack is big.",
      "That 3 in Midnight Baseball costs more than it's worth right now — the equity swing doesn't clear the price.",
      "Correct fold, wrong card. I've made peace with that sentence more times than I'd like.",
      "I'm not tilted. I'm doing the thing where I check whether I'm tilted, which from the outside looks identical.",
      "Let the record show I called that a mistake before I saw what it turned into.",
      "You're due for nothing. The deck has no memory and, frankly, neither should you.",
      "That's a lovely story about your lucky seat. I have fourteen years of mortality tables that disagree with the premise.",
      "I folded a winner. I'd fold it again tomorrow with the same three cards showing.",
      "The pot's enormous. The math is still the math — size doesn't get a vote.",
      "Small sample. Small sample. Say it with me — small sample.",
      "I logged that as a correct call that lost. I don't get to log it any other way just because it stings.",
      "Somebody remind me in an hour whether that river was actually rare or just felt rare.",
      "I'm fine. I'm just doing arithmetic where my face used to be.",
    ],
