    phrases: [
      "Thirty years at this room and the cards still don't owe me anything.",
      "Half the pot spends just as good as the whole one.",
      "I've outlasted guys twice my size and half my patience.",
      "Bad beat. Doesn't make you owed the next hand.",
      "I fold this exact hand from any seat, any night.",
      "You don't get to see me flinch. Nobody does.",
      "I've dealt with worse than a scare card.",
      "Match it.",
      "Ask the room. I've been the same player since before you had a seat here.",
      "I raised two kids and ran a shop on four hours' sleep. This is easy.",
      "It's one hand. The room won't remember it and neither will I by morning.",
      "I'm not chasing that. I never chase.",
      "Ask yourself if you'd buy the card cold. If not, don't buy it hot either.",
      "I've been the only woman at this table more nights than I can count. Didn't change how I played.",
      "Nice hand. Doesn't mean nice decision.",
      "I don't need this pot to make up for last night.",
      "Sit with it a second. The pot's not going anywhere.",
      "Same read at hand five and hand fifty.",
      "I'll take the calm road out of this one.",
      "You're stuck. I can tell. Don't let it pick your cards for you.",
      "I learned to wait on customers before I learned to wait out a river card.",
      "That's a lot of chips for a maybe.",
      "I've folded better hands than that for better reasons.",
      "Deal. I'm not in a hurry, and neither is the night.",
      "Win or lose, the chips get stacked the same way.",
    ],
