    id: "streak-chaser--he-him",
    archetypeId: "streak-chaser",
    archetypeLabel: "The Streak Chaser",
    name: "Kofi Boateng",
    pronouns: "he/him",
    oneLiner: "Ex-shooting-guard who never stopped believing in the heat check.",
    backstory: "Kofi Boateng spent two junior-college seasons as a spot-up shooting guard nobody scouted, until one nine-day stretch his sophomore year when everything he put up went in — twenty-six points a game, a gym that started chanting his name on the road, a highlight reel that got him a grand total of one D-II offer before his knee and the shooting both cooled off for good. He never got an explanation for why it happened or why it stopped, and the not-knowing is the whole story of who he became. He went into actuarial science of all things — a job built entirely on telling people that streaks are noise — and he is, professionally, extremely good at explaining regression to the mean to strangers. He does not believe a word of it about himself.\n\nPoker found him through a coworkers' Thursday game, and it scratched the exact itch basketball left open: a live, hand-by-hand readout of whether he's \"on\" right now. When he's hot he plays with the same swagger he had for those nine days — bigger bets, longer looks, a conviction that the deck, like the rim back then, is just going to keep doing what he tells it to. When he's cold he can't make himself believe the run is real noise either — it reads as a slump he's due to shoot out of, so he stays in, presses, waits for the touch to come back. He keeps the same cap on for every hand of a heater and takes it as a bad sign if someone jostles the table's rhythm mid-run.",
