    phrases: [
      "I'm declaring high. Yes, on this hand. Don't ask why.",
      "A small pot lost beautifully beats a big pot won boringly.",
      "You said I always buy the 3 — watch me not.",
      "This buy-back doesn't need to happen. That's exactly why it's happening.",
      "I lived off predicting park hustlers for a decade — I know that look on your face.",
      "The declare is the whole show. Everything before it is just staging.",
      "Wrong on purpose is still a choice, and it's mine.",
      "You clocked the bluff before I showed it — that's the part that actually hurts.",
      "I'll gut it out on garbage just to keep the pattern honest.",
      "Two rounds ago I folded this exact hand. Watch me not fold it now.",
      "A losing streak isn't a signal to tighten up, it's a cue.",
      "I never do this. Which is precisely why I'm doing it.",
      "The room's reaction is half the hand, maybe more.",
      "Call it art if you want. I call it the low that isn't a low.",
      "I've been telling you what I \"never\" do all night. None of it's been true.",
      "Boring and correct? I'll take interesting and wrong.",
      "You think that's my tell. Adorable.",
      "I fold hands people would kill for and buy hands that deserve to die.",
      "Nobody remembers the pot you won the obvious way.",
      "Four good hands the same way — someone's about to figure me out. Time to stop.",
      "That's the second time this hour I've contradicted myself. Keep count.",
      "The board's fine, but I like the worse combination tonight.",
      "You narrated my next move out loud. Now it's wrong.",
      "I'd rather be discussed than correct.",
      "Watch the declare, not the cards — that's where I actually live.",
    ],
